        <p>BOWLING.</p>
        <p>Warrington Cemetery Hotel Subscription \ Club. The return match in Use ht.me and home engage *tent with the Wigan Subscription Club, was played at Warrington on Saturday, when the home team was• captained by Mr S Taylor, tke visitors having Mr J T Pattord in that capacity. Warrington had a deficiency of 102 points to wipe out, having been beaten to this extent on the visitors green. The contest wag exciting Warrington just securing a victory by three points on, the two engagements. After the match the tesms a.d friends sat down to an excellent tea.' The remaider of the evening was spent in an enjoyable manner with, songs and toasts. Mr S Taylor occupied the chair. being supported by Mr Petford, and a good programme was gone through, which was much appreciated, Mr Brown recited "Old Pinder," and " People with talk ":. Mr T Humphreys sang, "I fear no foe ' and " Queen' of the earth " ; Mr J Draper, " Star of Bethlehem " anal "Mary of Argyle " ; Mr Longsbaw, " Honor's call "and " Bandolero "; Mr E Sanders recited " Liverwing' testimonial "and "Nomination Day " ; Mr McLoughlin, " Parody on Just before the Battle, Maher" ; Mr , Monday, " Rum Bons Bay " : Mr T Wilding, " Ever of. , thee" ; and Mr Ambrose, " The laughing tong," foe Chairman gave the toast of the evening, " 'the - visitors," which was responded to by Mr Petford.. Messrs Amos and Ambrose accompanied the songs mos: ably. WARRINGTON. WIGAN. $ Taylor (captain) H Williams II Taylor 2l J Brindle 2 Allison J Woods 2l If Davies W Hughes l5 T Wilding T Potter 2l W Langsbaw . 12 T Bolton 2l J Lowe ..... .............. .... 11: J A Jones ...., 2l J Boond 'P Si 111 s o n J Willett J Hewitt G Ball 2 Harrison 2l 2 Whatley .., ~ 13, TAnios .......... ................ 12 G Deeley 1 T Humphreys --` 309 20t4</p>
