        <head>PROPOSED NEW RESERVOIR AT DARESBURY.</head>
        <p>PROPOSED NEW RESERVOIR AT DARESBURY.</p>
        <p>- At a meeting of the Water Committen.it was resolved that a strip of land, containing about 256 Eq3a"e yards, in Delph-tane, in front of the new Pumping Stela:it be given to the Distrie; Council for the purpose of widen— ing the road, provided they make a suitable footpath to the satisfactmn of the engineer. The Water Engineer, reported that thvte was only about a month's stock of water in the Appleton reset voir,and it was resolved that the engineer be instructed to proceed with a preliminary survey for the preparations of plane for the new reser- v3ir at Daresbury ; and proceed with the work of laying a 3-inch main along Delph-lan3 to supply the watering trouzhs on the Myddloton Hall and Broadhurst's Trustees Estates.—At a meeting WI on the 16:h Sep- tembtr, the following letter from the Warrington Rural District Council was read :7—Sarveyor's Offs. Bewsey Chambers, Warrington, September 120 h, 1901. Dear Sir,—Delpt-lane improvement. Very many thanks for</p>
