      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-10-04_WidnesExaminer_art0061" n="art0061">
        <head>EARLESTOWN &amp; NEWTON</head>
        <p>EARLESTOWN &amp; NEWTON</p>
        <p>POLICE CASES. At the police station, Earlestown, on Monday morning before Mr J W Emmett, Patrick Burke and Hugh Jones of Earlestown were cnarged with being drunk and disorderly and were each fined 2.4 61 and costs.</p>
        <p>NEWTON CONGREGATIONAL CHURCH ORGANIST, Mr J F Knight. of ‘Viozan, who for three and a half years has cfficiated with conspicuous success as organist and choirmaster at the Congregational Church, Newton, severed his connection with that place of worship on Sunday evening. After the usual service a few musical items were given by the choir and organist and at the close the Rev James AlLatt snolre in a very feeling manner of the departure of Mr linight, and eulogised highly the services that gentleman had rendered to the church He expressed a fervent hope.that he would do well in his new sphere at St, Paul's C]ogregational Church, IVigan, to which he had been appointed organist.</p>
