      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-10-04_WidnesExaminer_art0074" n="art0074">
        <p>Swinton v Hunsiet.</p>
        <p>This match decw a large number of spectators to the Swinton ground, as it was the first League match that Swinton had played at horns. A Goldtoorp kicked a capital penalty goal. A few minutes later, however, Traynor equalised the score with a penalty goal. Then a combineu pas3ing movement by toe Swinton backs ended in bowls scoring a try behind the posts and Traynor kicked an easy goal. Nothing daunted, A Unlithorp go: away from a 9 •rummage, dodged s!,veral ot the Swiuton backq, End then passed toe ball out to Hannah, who scored a try for Hunslet near 031 corner flag. A. Goldthorp took toe place kick, scored a goal from the touch line, and made the s :ore again level. Swinton then attacked strongly, and from a DAS4 by Valentine, Jones scored ah on improved try. R sult : Swinton, two goa's and two tries (10 points) ; two goals and one try (seven points).</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-10-04_WidnesExaminer_art0075" n="art0075">
        <head>Batley v. Hull.</head>
        <p>Batley v. Hull.</p>
        <p>Played at Batlev, Driscoll made a splendid attempt to cross the Batley line. Jacques was awarded a tree kick for off-side, and obtained a goal. After this Batley played with betrer judgment, and took the ball the length of the field, Oakland scoring a try, but Davies failed at goal. Play continued for a time at the centre uutil Townend, by smart footwork, reached the Hull 25. The Batley forwards rushed the ball over the line, and Spurr credited his side with a try. Ralf-time score Battey, eight points ;Eiitl,two points. Driscoll crossed his opponents' line, Jacques failing at goal. Immedi- ately afterwards Elamort-cht, getting possession at the Batley quarter line made off, scored a try,and this time Jacques was succesgful at goal. After this the ball was taken the lengto of the field by the Batley forwards,and Oakland passing to Auty enabled that player to score a try, but Davies just missed at goal. Result :—Batley, one goal and three tries (eleven points) ; Hall, two goals and two trips (ten p -Ants).</p>
