        <p>Warrington "A " Defeated by Runcorn `• A.' Warrington " "team sustained another defeat on Saturday when tney eaclunted Itunenro "A "at lr well- lane. The vi si:artei, and Weston returning, a scrummage was formed in the centre. From this Moran secured, and ran in flue stsde to the v sitors line, where be was held up This placed Runcorn :on the aggres- sive, and they were still att.icking when the halt-time whistle was aounded. The fine play of the visitors' full-back aiicounted for their line b3ing kept iratact. On the re-sca:t; a p)ssing taut between Wiiliams. Parr and Moran saw the latter se ire. Wilkinson kick)cl a goal. Tile gam 4 now dev-Opei lot) an ia position of the.kick and rush style.neither side showing any rwric. Ituocorn had the bat of mar_tera,and retired winners by one goal one try to nil. Rano are " " have now played f aur matcher, won two, arid lo=t 2. While Warringtoa have played 3, lost 2, and drawn 1.</p>
