      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-10-04_WidnesExaminer_art0078" n="art0078">
        <head>Fletcher Russell's Easily Beaten</head>
        <p>Fletcher Russell's Easily Beaten</p>
        <p>Swinton "A " had tittle difficulty in deposing of Fletcher, Russell's at Warrington on Saturday. Potter started for the locals. Valentine made a fine run, but was brought up on the line. Imm4diately afterwards Walton scored. The goal kick failed. Forster ran well down the centre, but could no:: break th tough. Coopor was knocked down into touch within a yard of the line. Foden was conspicuous in sTaying a forward rush. Play settled in the Eigineers' quarter. Cooper, after beating all the horne.backs. s^orod. Valeatino failed at goal. The home backs made a grand passing move- ! meat, but co) ea4er play aooiled a good chance. The Lions again rittackd, Valentine being tackled on the lcoe• Cooper had a drop at goal, which failed by inchea, F:etchFr's again get going, but Forster failed to gather a pass from Foden, and a good chance was spoiled. fi,lf-tiree—Swinton "A " six points, Fletcher's nil. During the second half the visitors had again consid.r- ably the tpss r,ne garria, and Cooper proved. to bs in rare form, scoring three cries, improving on one so that ' the final mewl read-3 vinton "A " oaa goal floe tries 17 polo's) to Fletcher Russell's nil.</p>
