        <p>Warrington Sustain Defeat at Newton.</p>
        <p>Warringtm engaged in a Friendly match with Newton on Saturday afternoon. The match took place at Newton bef)re a poor attendance. Warriogtoa woo th 3 toss, and Mayar started hr New-,9, who ran down. but Ellis checked the ruth, and W orinzton dribbled up to Homeks, vho.was defeated Uy L'pihain in the first minute. Warrin..!tln came up again, but the Newton back i were nyr". to b caught napping a second time,and to liomegters drove them nick to their own goal Npwtort afterwola had the b!st of the game up to the interval, bat all their efforts to break through the Warrington cil'Adel Proved uav iliri. Hali—:ime : Warrington( one gla/. Nlwton nil. D 'nine the second hcf Newton hi tde wail in their favour and claimed the rnaj or portion of the att(ek, goala b iog recorded by Kenny, Mayor and Billiugton, the liorne team winning by three goata to one. LANCASHIRE LEAGUE.</p>
