        <p>A VOLUNTEER CONUNDRUIf.—The E srl of Stair was present the other day. with Lieutenant-General Sir Archibald Rueter, who was his guest, at the opening of the new drill Hall at Stranraer by Sir Archibald, and distributed medals to the active service company of the Galloway Rifles. His lordship remarked that it was forty-two years since he joined the volunteers, and in those far.back days a good many joke were current at their expense. There vms one in the torm of a conundruna,lnough it was hardly:applicable nowadays tt How are the volunteers like old maids ?" " Because they are always ready and never wanted.' REMARKABLE EFFECT OF A DROTIOEIT.—The summer's drought has caused a somewhat curious spectacle to make its appearance near Bolton. At Turton, the Bolton Corporation's reservoir has been rapidly drying up, and now the roofs and chircheye of houves are to be seen above the water. The reservoir was formed in a natural valley, and the people inhabiting the houses therein refused to leave until they were absolutely eempellad to do FO bv the water. This is the first time that the houEes havebeen seen sinos their first disap- pearance.</p>
